A||||29||Black86SE||The Day My Engine Was Removed||||1||
Z||000000||Black86SE||11-05-2001||12:05 AM||||Saturday FieroJoe and I removed my engine so I can do a tranny swap and to paint it. It only took us about 9 hours which is a lot less than I thought it would take due to the fact that neither of us has done this before. If you have any questions feel free to ask. These are some pics of the day. Sorry if they are slow.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fluiddrain2.gif"> <BR>Here we are draining the fluids that need draining. Coolant, fuel, more coolant, and a little bit of coolant. (never seemed to stop coming out) We disconnected the wires from the ECM and pulled them through the firewall and disconnected the cables. Unbolted everything that needed to be unbolted in the engine compartment. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_puller2.gif"> <BR>This is the engine puller that we used. It was huge. That is FieroJoe showing how big that hoist was.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/getting_ready2.gif"> <BR>Here I am looking lost next to my car. I was watching to make sure that nothing was binding or getting caught while the car was being lifted.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/air_fiero2.gif"> <BR>My car getting major air. The rear bumper was probably 4 feet off the ground while the front bumper was more like 1 inch off the ground.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joe_in_enginecomp2.gif"> <BR>OH NO! Joe is being eaten by the car. Oh wait, he is just disconnecting some things we forgot. Whew!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine-rear2.gif"> <BR>Well, here it is. Looks a lot bigger out of the car. This is a shot of the rear.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine-front2.gif"> <BR>This is a shot of the front. Kinda dirty, but it will be cleaned up and painted.<P>Like I stated above, feel free to ask any questions if you have any.<P>------------------<BR>Black 1986 V6 SE<BR>17" Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS<BR>AIM ScreenName: Black86se||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroKyle||11-05-2001||12:11 AM||||probably wish ya had a 350 laying around, huh? lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black86SE||11-05-2001||12:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>probably wish ya had a 350 laying around, huh? lol   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well actually, I have a 350. But not laying around. It is kinda attatched to my truck. And I am attatched to my truck. Hmmm, would I notice if I switched a 350 for a 173? YES!||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroKyle||11-05-2001||12:40 AM||||"All goood questions." - 6 days, 7 nights  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||11-05-2001||01:07 AM||||While your engine is out, Id replace the forward exhaust manifold w/a known good one, whether it needs it or not. Believe me, you dont want to have to replace that thing while its still in the car!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Id go on and replace the plugs to, might as well while everything is so easily accesable.<BR>As far as engine removal, any words of wisdom? Any do's and donts? Things that caused probs? Im curious, thanks.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black86SE||11-05-2001||01:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>While your engine is out, Id replace the forward exhaust manifold w/a known good one, whether it needs it or not. Believe me, you dont want to have to replace that thing while its still in the car!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Id go on and replace the plugs to, might as well while everything is so easily accesable.<BR>As far as engine removal, any words of wisdom? Any do's and donts? Things that caused probs? Im curious, thanks.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I replaced the plugs this summer with no probs. We didn't have any problems other than instead of losening a cradle bolt we were tightening it and using a cheater bar which ended up breaking a 15mm socket. Oh yeah, don't disconnect each individual sensor from the engine, disconnect the wiring from the ECM and pull it through the firewall, hell of a lot easier. Let the front of the cradle down first and support it on something like wood. Then lower the back. Just make sure you can get the cradle out from under the car. Use some sort of rolling pallet. We didn't, and we regret it and have to build one now.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||11-05-2001||01:53 AM||||black86se, thanks for doing the post. <P>Keep us updated when you swap the trans and any problems you come up with.  <P>I looked at my fiero, and saw where the master for the clutch will go.  It seems i have to knock out the metal slug.  I also looked at my service manual, and i think the only difficult part is setting up the shifter.<P><BR>Did you lift your car by lifting the engine which brought the car 4 feet high?<P>When it was up, then did you support the car with jacks, then dropped the cradle?||||reg||1
Z||000007||jch82||11-05-2001||03:31 AM||||Now I know who to talk to when I do my engine swap!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>I plan on putting a camaro 3.4 in sometime before spring. As of right now, its all plans...<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_2.jpg"> ||||reg||14
