Z||000012||MooCow||11-05-2001||12:29 PM||||Look at all the fun I missed out on.  Thats okay at least I have a few more people that will help me next year when I put my new tranny in.  I would have came out but I moved my car out of the shed and started working on it so I didnt make it out.<BR>When do you plan on putting it back in??<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||10
Z||000013||PAUL88GT||11-05-2001||01:03 PM||||Good job.  If had my engine out, I would replace the water pump while it is easy to get to all the bolts. Just a suggestion.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Black86SE||11-05-2001||03:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierospeeder:<BR><B>Did you lift your car by lifting the engine which brought the car 4 feet high?<P>When it was up, then did you support the car with jacks, then dropped the cradle?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>To lift the car we got all the stuff disconnected in the engine compartment, then we removed the nuts that hold the strut towers on and picked up the car by hand high enough to let the studs come out. Then we used a 5/16" chain about 5' long and a grade 8 bolt with a nut on each end. We put the bolt through the bigest hole of the three from the strut tower and put a nut underneath. Then we supported the front of the cradle with some wood underneath. Then used a floor jack on the rear of the cradle to support that. We removed the bolts holding on the front of the cradle and let it rest on the wood. Then we removed the bolts on the rear of the cradle and once they were removed we left it supported by the wood and floor jack. Then we used the engine hoist to lift the car being oh so careful not to rip anything off the engine on the way up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||The Fieromaster||11-05-2001||03:33 PM||||Does Joe ever smile?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">         <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                 <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
