Z||000019||BN Boomer||11-06-2001||05:18 PM||||Do you guys do EVERYTHING the hard way?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://wsphotofews.excite.com/004/fL/xH/mZ/IO51930.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Black86SE||11-06-2001||05:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>Do you guys do EVERYTHING the hard way?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have read and talked to some people and they have said that it is easier to remove the engine with the cradle from underneath rather than just pulling just the engine from the top. Removing the engine and cradle was the easy part, it was disconnecting all the other stuff first that took the most time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||fierospeeder||11-06-2001||05:55 PM||||and i thought i was the only one.<P>When you buy a fiero, you have to buy an engine hoist.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Black86SE||11-10-2001||07:40 PM||||Just an update on my progress. Today Joe and I finished making the cart to roll the cradle around on, we removed the wiring harness for the engine. Pulled off the A/C compressor, pulled the manifolds, plenum, fuel rail, lower plenum, and heads. When I got home I started to clean up the upper and lower plenum, valve covers, and intake manifold. I forgot my camera today so I don't have any pics of the engine but I have pics of the parts. I probably won't post those though. Everything came apart very easily. The head bolts were the only bolts that were tough. I will keep updating this. See-ya!<P>------------------<BR>Black 1986 V6 SE<BR>17" Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS<BR>AIM ScreenName: Black86se||||reg||1
Z||000023||jelly2m8||11-10-2001||09:44 PM||||Heres a side view.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/come%20out%20biotch!.BMP"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||SLYGUY||11-10-2001||10:46 PM||||How are you guys raising the rear end of the cars like that?<BR>I don't have a problem buying an engine hoist but I can't see in the pictures how you guys are getting the car up like that.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000025||jelly2m8||11-10-2001||10:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>How are you guys raising the rear end of the cars like that?<BR>I don't have a problem buying an engine hoist but I can't see in the pictures how you guys are getting the car up like that.<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i use a chain from the drivers strut tower to the dog bone mount.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||FieroMontreal||11-10-2001||11:28 PM||||OMG! THOSE CARS ARE FLYING!<P>LMAO, That car on a stack of wood is the funniest thing I've ever seen! Good work!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>-Alex President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> ||||reg||1
