Z||000028||avengador1||11-11-2001||10:07 AM||||The secret is you jack the car up a bit at a time and keep stacking supports underneath till you reach the desired height.If you notice in my picture the car is on jackstands that are on blocks of cement.||||reg||1
Z||000029||wkayl||11-11-2001||10:21 AM||||Just a note, cement blocks are not very strong when set in a way you can see through the holes.  Wooden blocks are much safer. <P>P.S.  I have used cement blocks in the past. Haven't we all?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">   <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
